    <system:String
        x:Key="MepSettingsWindow.MinSizesTooltip">
        For example, if there is a cable tray with width 300 and height 50,
by setting minimum height to 50 and minimum width to 300,
openings will be created only for trays
with width >= 300 and height >= 50.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="MepSettingsWindow.MinSizesLabel">Minimum element dimensions, mm</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="MepSettingsWindow.RoundingsLabel">Rounding, mm</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="MepSettingsWindow.RoundingsTooltip">
        For example, if a pipe with diameter 110 passes through a wall and Clearance=50 and Rounding=50 mm are set,
an opening with diameter 200 mm will be created,
since the opening diameter with clearances of 50 mm becomes 110+2*50=210 mm,
after which it will be rounded according to mathematical rules to multiples of 50 mm, i.e. to 200 mm.</system:String>
