    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Incoming.UnacceptableConstructions.Title">Unacceptable constructions check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Incoming.UnacceptableConstructions.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">Checks whether the opening task intersects "Structural Framing" or "Structural Columns" of the current file. Status: "Unacceptable structures".

If disabled, such tasks go through the remaining checks as usual; a task located only in a beam or a column gets "No intersection".</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Incoming.Intersections.Title">Task completion check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Incoming.Intersections.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">Determines what the opening task intersects in the current file: constructions only — "New task", constructions and real openings — "Partially completed task", real openings only — "Completed task", nothing — "No intersection".

If disabled, every task gets the "New task" status, and the nested different constructions check and host search are disabled too.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Incoming.DifferentConstructions.Title">Different constructions check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Incoming.DifferentConstructions.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">Checks whether the constructions of the current file intersected by the task, including the hosts of intersected real openings, belong to different categories — for example, walls and floors. Status: "In different structures".

If disabled, tasks at a wall and floor junction get a regular completion status.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Incoming.Host.Title">Host search</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Incoming.Host.Description">Determines the construction of the current file that the task is located in: the host of the intersected real opening or, if there is none, the construction with the largest intersection volume. Assigns no status: fills the "Host" column in the Navigator.</system:String>

    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Real.NotActual.Title">Actuality check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Real.NotActual.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">Checks whether the real opening fully covers the incoming tasks and MEP elements from links that intersect it: if they go beyond the opening and intersect its host, the opening is outdated. Status: "Outdated opening".

If disabled, the nested fill check is disabled too, and all openings except too close ones in structural files get the "Correct" status — including outdated ones.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Real.VolumeMatch.Title">Opening fill check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Real.VolumeMatch.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">Determines what share of the real opening volume is occupied by incoming tasks and MEP elements from links: less than the "empty" threshold — "Empty opening", less than the "too big" threshold — "Opening is too big".

If disabled, openings are considered correct.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Real.VolumeMatch.EmptyPercent">"Empty" threshold, % of intersected volume</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Real.VolumeMatch.TooBigPercent">"Too big" threshold, % of intersected volume</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Real.TooClose.Title">Distance between openings check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Real.TooClose.Description">Checks whether another structural real opening is closer than the specified distance to the edges of the opening in the construction plane. Status: "Openings are too close to each other".</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Real.TooClose.DistanceValue">Minimum distance, mm</system:String>

    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.ManuallyPlaced.Title">Manual placement check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.ManuallyPlaced.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">Checks whether the "ФОП_Размещено вручную" parameter of the opening task is enabled. Status: "Placed manually".

If disabled, such tasks go through the remaining checks as usual and may get a size or actuality error status.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.NotActual.Title">Actuality check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.NotActual.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">The task is outdated if no MEP element intersects it, if no link contains a construction the task is located in, or if MEP elements outside the task intersect this construction or a real opening from the link. Status: "Outdated task".

If disabled, the nested different constructions check is disabled too, the host search gets slower, and tasks without MEP elements get "Geometry processing error" when the offsets check is enabled.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.DifferentConstructions.Title">Different constructions check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.DifferentConstructions.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">Checks whether the link constructions the task is located in belong to different categories — for example, walls and floors. Status: "In different structures".

If disabled, tasks at a wall and floor junction go through the remaining checks as usual.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.Host.Title">Host search</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.Host.Description">Determines the link construction the task is located in: the one intersecting at least half of the task volume or, if there is none, the one with the largest intersection volume. Assigns no status: the host is needed to highlight it on the view when the task is selected in the Navigator. Works faster if the actuality check is enabled: it already finds the candidate constructions.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.UnacceptableConstructions.Title">Unacceptable constructions check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.UnacceptableConstructions.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">Checks whether the opening task intersects "Structural Framing" or "Structural Columns" from links. Status: "Unacceptable structures".

If disabled, such tasks go through the remaining checks as usual.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.Intersects.Title">Intersection with other tasks check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.Intersects.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">Checks whether the opening task intersects another opening task of the current file. Status: "Intersecting task".

If disabled, the intersection is not marked, and such tasks get a union or offsets status.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.United.Title">Union check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.United.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">Checks whether two or more MEP elements pass through the opening task. Status: "United".

If disabled, united tasks almost always get "Task is too big": the offsets check compares the task with a single element only.</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.Offsets.Title">Offsets check</system:String>
    <system:String
        x:Key="NavigatorSettings.Outcoming.Offsets.Description"
        xml:space="preserve">Compares the sum of the task offsets from the MEP element (top and bottom, left and right) with the double clearance from the placement settings, taking rounding into account: less — "Task is too small", more — "Task is too big".

Offsets are measured against a single element, so for united tasks the result is correct only together with the union check, and for tasks without MEP elements — only together with the actuality check. If disabled, tasks are considered correct.</system:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
